                         WILLIAM THE BUCCANEER

  You missed the turn deadline. The computer ordered Defend actions for your
generals. If we receive a late move, we will process it and send you the turn
results. If you miss 2 turns, the computer will drop you from the game.





  Quote of the Week:

  Saint Ignatius Loyola, Spanish soldier and founder of the Jesuit Order, 
1522:
  "To arrive at the truth in all things, we ought always to be ready to 
believe that what seems to us white, is black if the hierarchical Church so 
defines it."


ACTION REPORT    

Here's what happened to Your Majesty this turn:

  Frigid winter melted into spring, and William made ready to carry out his 
urgent orders.  He prepared his forces to defend Sumatra and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thus endeth the adventures of William the Buccaneer for this year.


  Your Majesty, I have news to report of wanderers in our kingdom:  
  The 30th Bowmen helped a local earl of Sumatra to subdue a native tribe 
and rose to Veteran quality.


  Here is the financial report for William's kingdom: this turn, the Kingdom 
collected 0 gold in revenue.  0 gold was expended to finance our leaders.  0 
gold was expended to maintain our armies.  William was left with 0 gold in 
the treasury.


LETTER REPORTS

  O King of Kings, thy heroes have travelled around the globe in
search of adventure and conquest.  I have faithfully kept their
correspondence, and now I present it to thee:


From: Dreux
To: William

  Honored Sovereign, 

  In spring, I prepared my forces to defend Borneo and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Dreux


From: Eustace
To: William

  Honored Sovereign, 

  With the coming of the spring season, I set out to quench my thirst for 
glory.  I prepared my armies to defend Malaysia and the surrounding 
provinces.

  Thy humble servant,   Eustace


